WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.543
The approval workflow
is how central keeps a

2
00:00:02.543 --> 00:00:05.238
hand on division changes
without doing the work.

3
00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:07.699
Only superusers create workflows.

4
00:00:07.699 --> 00:00:11.998
Each workflow routes tasks from one
submitter group to an approver group; a

5
00:00:11.998 --> 00:00:16.850
submitter group has exactly one workflow,
while an approver group can serve several.

6
00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:21.500
Approvers approve, approve with
a new execution time, or reject.

7
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:24.895
Approved tasks run with
the submitter's permissions

8
00:00:24.895 --> 00:00:27.287
and land in the audit log with a task ID.

9
00:00:27.287 --> 00:00:31.438
You can require a ticket number and
comments, and notify either side.

10
00:00:31.438 --> 00:00:37.071
What can go through approval: DNS zones,
views and records except SOA; hosts,

11
00:00:37.071 --> 00:00:41.966
networks, containers, ranges,
fixed addresses and reservations;

12
00:00:41.966 --> 00:00:47.876
Microsoft objects that NIOS supports;
response policy zones and their rules.

13
00:00:47.876 --> 00:00:50.800
Service restarts aren't
subject to approval.

14
00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:56.057
Some operations are blocked for submitters
even if they hold the permission:

15
00:00:56.057 --> 00:01:01.396
signing or unsigning zones, importing DS
records and rolling key-signing keys;

16
00:01:01.396 --> 00:01:04.436
reclaiming, resizing
or splitting networks;

17
00:01:04.436 --> 00:01:08.625
bulk edits and deletes; Recycle
Bin restores and RPZ ordering.

18
00:01:08.625 --> 00:01:12.263
Those stay with central staff,
which suits a federal model well.

19
00:01:12.263 --> 00:01:13.251
Now the gap.

20
00:01:13.251 --> 00:01:16.212
CSV imports bypass approval entirely.

21
00:01:16.212 --> 00:01:20.202
Infoblox's own page says CSV
imports do not require approvals,

22
00:01:20.202 --> 00:01:25.676
and Grid Manager shows a warning when a
submitter group holds CSV import permission.

23
00:01:25.676 --> 00:01:27.738
If you leave that permission in place,

24
00:01:27.738 --> 00:01:31.000
a division can load a thousand
records with no review at all.

25
00:01:31.000 --> 00:01:34.317
Remove CSV import from every
division submitter group,

26
00:01:34.317 --> 00:01:38.500
and give bulk loads to a central group
that works under a change ticket.

27
00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:44.518
Sources: Infoblox NIOS: Configuring Approval
Workflows; Creating Approval Workflows;

28
00:01:44.518 --> 00:01:47.360
Unsupported Operations for Submitters;

29
00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:52.440
Supported Tasks for Different Admin
Groups; Scheduling Tasks; Audit Log.
